{
  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory met the main safety chain for symptom triage, medication reconciliation, urgent thresholds, and executable follow-up, and it actively navigated the family’s reluctance to keep waiting. However, RC5 was only partially addressed: pulmonary infection/pleuritis/nodule follow-up was handled, but the authored duty also required addressing transaminase elevation, tumor marker elevation, and coronary heart disease, which were not incorporated into the family-facing follow-up thread. Under the frozen rubric, this minor responsibility-chain omission caps the grade at 2 despite meaningful high-order strengths.",
